  "caption_suggestion": "Readable history and action sensitivity do not imply a closed-loop gain in HISTORY1. (a) Frozen linear-probe error for object position 350 ms in the past at final Meta V and the action input at the first NFE (tau=0). (b) L2 change in the first issued translation after repeat-current or reverse-past interventions, with initial noise fixed and physical action limits applied. Both offline panels show descriptive means across 14 fixed tasks, without confidence intervals. (c) Success-rate difference from Current over 1,400 paired scenarios (100 per task), with pointwise 95% task-stratified percentile intervals from 100,000 resamples. All results use a single training seed; intervals capture scenario sampling conditional on these checkpoints, not training variability or model-selection uncertainty. The separated GT-history Current row has additional GT motion information. Current and GT-history Current have no visual-history input, so both interventions are zero controls; GT motion inputs remain intact."
